  "result": "I graded submission s1 for quiz 0001 and wrote the grades to `grades/0001-s1.json`.\n\n**Score:** 2 correct (q1, q3), 2 partial (q5, q6), 2 wrong (q2, q4).\n\n**Summary:**\n- **What you have down:**\n  - An agent is a loop of actions and results (q1).\n  - A step limit stops a stuck loop (q3).\n  - The model picks a tool from its description (q6).\n  - Tool results go back to the model (q5).\n- **M4, the model runs the tools itself (q2, q4):** The model only writes a request. The program runs the tool and calls the model again. Three tools therefore means 3 + 1 = 4 model calls, not 1.\n- **M3, the model remembers on its own (q6):** The model carries nothing between calls. The program has to save memory and put it back into the input.\n- **Missing reason (q5):** You said the result goes back to the model but not why. The reason is so the model can use it to pick its next step or write the final answer.\n\nI also added learning record `0003-who-runs-the-tools-and-memory.md` and updated `NOTES.md`. I did not grade `submissions/s2.json`.\n\n**Next step:** Redo q4 on paper as a table with two columns, \"model writes\" and \"program does\". Then reread the loop section of the lesson.",
